/7/labels","id":453043,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNDUzMDQz","number":7,"title":"3.0.0","description":"New major release that breaks compatibility with 2.x\r\n\r\n- PHP5.4.19+\r\n- New ORM & behaviors.\r\n- Improved Routing\r\n- PSR-0 and composer support.\r\n- Simpler configuration and bootstrapping.\r\n- Improved configuration handling.\r\n- Improved bake.\r\n\r\nSee [the roadmap](http://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/wiki/3.0-roadmap) for more details.","creator":null,"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":2464,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-10-11T20:56:23Z","updated_at":"2015-12-17T03:00:48Z","due_on":"2015-03-22T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-03-23T01:02:41Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2014-10-29T16:01:36Z","updated_at":"2014-10-30T01:39:05Z","closed_at":"2014-10-30T01:38:55Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Currently the command for executing composer to dump the autoloader (https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/d5a189d3f8f2c40c5ed1672a1e993e5911455d17/src/Shell/Task/PluginTask.php#L267-L268) uses a `;` to separate the `cd` and `php` commands, however this isn't supported on the regular Windows CLI, only Powershell supports it.\n\nThe Windows equivalent to `;` would be `&`, which in turn doesn't work in Powershell , but I'm pretty sure most people with Windows dev environments are using the regular shell. `&&` would work too, however I'm note sure whether the path can be expected to always be an absolute one, ie whether the `cd` command can be expected to not fail.\n","closed_by":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/